{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795328086,"nonce":"lKfLg+mo8sAyaBwwNfvHoIy3m8Y=","title":"Log tail: the first read after a kubelet log rotation stores no marker","message":"Deferred from the 0.7.0 review (b2-judge T-2). When the kubelet rotates a container log between two reads, the next read starts in the new file and the bytes in the rotated file are not stored; the kubelet log API gives no signal that a rotation happened, so no 'may be missing' marker is written. Needs a design change (e.g. compare the container's log file size/inode through the node API, or always mark a reopen after a long gap).","files":null}]}